{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kf2lkfklms7fs7ghoalcbtzevr7bf43i3qrx3whyejv7uecfedsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit with **one** exported symbol, `int call_predict(int pfcn)`, plus 14 `static` functions (a 17-arm generic sample predictor, 12 specialised predictors, and a `void*`-returning dispatcher). `call_predict` returns 1 iff `pfcn ∈ 0..=11`.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all in the crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` map. C exports exactly `call_predict`; Rust exports exactly `call_predict`. **Symbol diff empty in both directions**; 0 non-libc undefined symbols. Nothing was missing, so no C source needed translating (and no stubs were added). Also documents that `lib.h` declares `get_predict_func`, which *no* TU defines — correctly absent from both `.so`s. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 14 rows, derived mechanically (0 asserts, 0 `NULL` checks, 0 `if`s, 3 `default:` arms in the C). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 42 rows over 7 axes (entry point × `pfcn` × 8 ring phases × 10 `psamp` shapes × 8 `firfx` shapes × struct layout × build config). |\n\n## Phases B/C — differential tests (`tests/differential.rs`, 1346 lines)\n\n45 tests + 2 opt-in exhaustive sweeps, **all passing**. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and called only through `dlsym` — Rust is never called directly.\n\nBecause the C's internals are `static`, per-wrapper testing of only `call_predict` would leave 14 functions unverified. So two auxiliary shim libraries (built **outside** `c_src/`, which is unmodified — md5s confirmed) expose both TUs' internals: `tests/aux/aux_c.c` `#include`s `lib.c`, and `tests/aux/aux_rust_suffix.rs` is concatenated with `src/lib.rs` and compiled with `rustc`. That let me differentially test the low-level predictors, the dispatch-table mapping (via a language-neutral identity bitmap and call-through), and struct size/align/offsets.\n\nNotable: the C's deliberate quirks are preserved and verified — `case 10` uses `>>4` while `_Pfn10` uses `>>3`; `case 11` uses `>>3` while `_Pfn11` uses `>>1`. Inputs are magnitude-bounded (FIR coefficients auto-scaled) so no comparison ever relies on C signed-overflow UB.\n\n**Harness self-validation:** 7 behaviour-changing mutations injected into `src/lib.rs` were all detected by the expected test; 1 semantically-equivalent mutation was correctly not flagged. `src/lib.rs` was restored bit-identically (`diff` verified).\n\n## Phase D — parity, combos, completion gate\n\n- Symbol diff: empty. `phase_d_symbol_parity` asserts this in-suite.\n- `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** section ⇒ exactly 1 combination. `run_all_configs.sh` extracts features from `Cargo.toml`, enumerates the power set, and runs check+build+test for each × {debug, release}, plus `--all-features`, plus the symbol diff → **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED**, 0 warnings.\n- Extra hardening: suite also passes with the debug cdylib and `AUX_OVERFLOW_CHECKS=on` (Rust built with overflow-checks/debug-assertions ON — no panics where C wraps).\n- Exhaustive: `err_call_predict_exhaustive_every_i32` and `err_generic_predict_exhaustive_every_pfcn` compare **all 2³² `int` inputs** (36 s), so the exported API's input domain is covered without sampling.\n\nNo divergences were found, so `src/lib.rs` required no fixes; the only change to the crate was adding `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":135643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af066349-f3cc-4b00-bb3f-6e389d47f934","uuid":"0ab0f456-3971-42be-9767-59050e9f6595","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:04:44.947Z"}
